WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.180
Visiting teachers pass
through a small town.

2
00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:07.230
Each one praises his own
teaching and attacks the others.

3
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:10.540
The townspeople, the
Kalamas, are confused.

4
00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:13.670
They ask the Buddha:
who should we believe?

5
00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:17.430
Today a new voice joins
the argument: science.

6
00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:22.110
It finds no mechanism by which
moral actions shape future lives.

7
00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.530
So if science cannot
detect karma or rebirth,

8
00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:28.420
what should Buddhists
do with those beliefs?

9
00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:31.690
In this mission, you'll read
what the Buddha told the Kalamas,

10
00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:34.720
and see why Buddhists
still argue about it.

11
00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:37.750
Then you'll test Buddhist
beliefs against science,

12
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.400
from karma and rebirth
to stories of miracles.

13
00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:46.350
Your mission: weigh up how Buddhists
respond when science cannot detect karma

14
00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:47.390
or rebirth.
